		--flags-dir # Import flag values from a directory.
		--json @bool # Format output as json.
		--line-ending (CRLF|LF) # Line ending used in the CSV file. Default value on Windows is `CRLF`; on macOS and Linux it's `LF`.
		--sobject|-s # API name of the Salesforce object, either standard or custom, into which you're importing records.
		--target-org|-o # Username or alias of the target org. Not required if the `target-org` configuration variable is already set.
		--wait|-w # Time to wait for the command to finish, in minutes.
	data:import:resume # When the original "sf data import bulk" command times out, it displays a job ID.
		--flags-dir # Import flag values from a directory.
		--job-id|-i # Job ID of the bulk import.
		--json @bool # Format output as json.
		--use-most-recent @bool # Use the job ID of the bulk import job that was most recently run.
		--wait|-w # Time to wait for the command to finish, in minutes.
	data:import:tree # The JSON files that contain the data are in sObject tree format, which is a collection of nested, parent-child records with a single root record.
		--api-version # Override the api version used for api requests made by this command
		--files|-f # Comma-separated and in-order JSON files that contain the records, in sObject tree format, that you want to insert.
		--flags-dir # Import flag values from a directory.
		--json @bool # Format output as json.
		--loglevel
		--plan|-p # Unlike when you use the `--files` flag, the files listed in the plan definition file **can** contain more then 200 records. When the CLI executes the import, it automatically batches the records to comply with the 200 record limit set by the API.  The order in which you list the files in the plan definition file matters. Specifically, records with lookups to records in another file should be listed AFTER that file. For example, let's say you're loading Account and Contact records, and the contacts have references to those accounts. Be sure you list the Accounts file before the Contacts file.  The plan definition file has the following schema:  - items(object) - SObject Type: Definition of records to be insert per SObject Type   - sobject(string) - Name of SObject: Child file references must have SObject roots of this type   - files(array) - Files: An array of files paths to load
		--target-org|-o # Username or alias of the target org. Not required if the `target-org` configuration variable is already set.
	data:query # Specify the SOQL query at the command line with the --query flag or read the query from a file with the --file flag.  If your query returns more than 10,000 records, prefer to use the `sf data export bulk` command instead.
		--all-rows @bool # Include deleted records. By default, deleted records are not returned.
		--api-version # Override the api version used for api requests made by this command
		--file|-f # File that contains the SOQL query.
		--flags-dir # Import flag values from a directory.
		--json @bool # Format output as json.
		--loglevel
		--output-file # File where records are written; only CSV and JSON output formats are supported.
		--perflog @bool # Gets data on API performance metrics from the server. The data is stored in $HOME/.sfdx/apiPerformanceLog.json.
		--query|-q # SOQL query to execute.
