		--target-dev-hub|-v # Overrides the value of the target-dev-hub configuration variable, if set.
		--track-source|-t @bool # We recommend you enable source tracking in scratch orgs, which is why it's the default behavior. Source tracking allows you to track the changes you make to your metadata, both in your local project and in the scratch org, and to detect any conflicts between the two.  To disable source tracking in the new scratch org, specify the --no-track-source flag. The main reason to disable source tracking is for performance. For example, while you probably want to deploy metadata and run Apex tests in your CI/CD jobs, you probably don't want to incur the costs of source tracking (checking for conflicts, polling the SourceMember object, various file system operations.) This is a good use case for disabling source tracking in the scratch org.
