	package:install # To install or upgrade a package, specify a specific version of the package using the 04t package ID.
		--apex-compile|-a (all|package) # Applies to unlocked packages only. Specifies whether to compile all Apex in the org and package, or only the Apex in the package.  For package installs into production orgs, or any org that has Apex Compile on Deploy enabled, the platform compiles all Apex in the org after the package install or upgrade operation completes.  This approach assures that package installs and upgrades don’t impact the performance of an org, and is done even if --apex-compile package is specified.
		--api-version # Override the api version used for api requests made by this command
